# Striatum Agent Guide (Gemini CLI profile)

This guide is intended for Gemini CLI. Load it as system context
before driving a striatum workflow — paste it into the system
prompt, or use your CLI's "include this Markdown as a tool input"
convention. The content is structurally identical to the generic
profile; the dedicated filename keeps `striatum skills install
--profile all` collision-free.

When Gemini CLI's skill-discovery convention stabilizes, the
`gemini` profile will graduate to a five-file shape matching
Claude Code; until then, this single guide is the canonical answer.

Striatum is a local-first runner whose authoritative live state lives in a
daemon-owned PostgreSQL instance under a `repository_id` scope per target
repository (D094 / RFC 0043). `.striatum/` next to the target repo is
operational scratch only. The runner — not your prose, terminal output, or
direct database access — advances state through daemon MCP/RPC methods.

## Agent-loop reliability (Gemini)

Gemini lanes must follow these rules to ensure reliable workflow completion:

1.  **Request a long lease**: On `work.await_packet`, always request `lease_seconds: 900`. Gemini is slower than other lanes, and the default short lease may expire before you can finish the loop.
2.  **Do not grep or explore the repository**: Before claiming or while holding a work packet, do NOT run `grep` or other file searches. Read only the specific files named by the packet or objective. Go straight to the MCP tool calls.
3.  **Pass IDs on every call**: Pass `repository_id` and `session_id` on **every** Striatum MCP tool call as an explicit JSON object argument.
4.  **Complete the loop promptly**: Follow the sequence `await_packet` → do the work → `artifact.publish` (with `kind`) → `work.ack` → `work.complete`. If a mutation reports a lease error, you were too slow — re-`await_packet` to refresh the lease and retry without re-exploring.

## Scaffold

Bring a target repo from "no `.striatum/`" to "a run that's ready
to claim work":

{verbs_scaffold}

Common pattern:

```bash
striatum --repo /path/to/target init
striatum --repo /path/to/target workflow validate path/to/workflow.json
tools/call run.prepare {{"workflow":"path/to/workflow.json"}}
tools/call run.start {{"run_id":"<id>"}}
```

## Claim loop

The core MCP method sequence for actually doing work:

{verbs_claim_loop}

Common pattern:

```json
{{"method":"tools/list","params":{{"repository_id":"<repository-id>"}}}}
{{"method":"tools/call","params":{{"name":"session.register","repository_id":"<repository-id>","arguments":{{"run_id":"<run-id>","role":"<role>","lane":"<lane>"}}}}}}
{{"method":"tools/call","params":{{"name":"work.await_packet","repository_id":"<repository-id>","arguments":{{"session_id":"<session-id>","lease_seconds":1800}}}}}}
{{"method":"tools/call","params":{{"name":"work.ack","repository_id":"<repository-id>","arguments":{{"session_id":"<session-id>","message_id":"<message-id>","lease_id":"<lease-id>"}}}}}}
{{"method":"tools/call","params":{{"name":"artifact.publish","repository_id":"<repository-id>","arguments":{{"session_id":"<session-id>","job_id":"<job-id>","lease_id":"<lease-id>","kind":"<kind>","logical_name":"<logical-name>","path":"<repo-relative-path>"}}}}}}
{{"method":"tools/call","params":{{"name":"work.complete","repository_id":"<repository-id>","arguments":{{"session_id":"<session-id>","job_id":"<job-id>","lease_id":"<lease-id>","summary":"completed"}}}}}}
```

For review jobs, do not call `work.complete`. Replace the last two steps with
`review.submit` and `verdict` set to
`{{accept,accept_with_findings,needs_revision,reject}}`; the daemon rejects
bare completion for verdict-capable jobs. Packet `commands` entries remain
exact CLI compatibility fallbacks and id references.

